<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40356" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">raedārĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rēdārĭus</span></b> ), i,
			adj.
		raeda, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a four-wheeled
			carriage</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mulae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 17, 7</span></i>
			.— Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">raedārĭus</span></b> ,
				i, m.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A coachman</i>, <i>the driver of a
				ræda</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">raedarium occidunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Mil. 10, 29</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A wagon-builder</i>, <i>coachmaker</i>, Capitol. Max. et Balb. 5, § 1.</div>
